&lt;p&gt;unknown&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2 id="garden-description"&gt;Garden Description&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the other side of the fortified enceinte, one hundred and fifty kilometers &lt;!-- TODO: meters??? --&gt; south was a large building that belonged to an architect according to an inscription found near the peristyle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This huge suburban villa incompletely excavated, was laid out around two peristyles (Plan view, Fig. 1).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A large peristyle of twenty columns onto which rooms opened may have had a garden.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;On the south of the peristyle was another courtyard with a portico of three columns on the east and west sides. The courtyard may have been planted.&lt;/p&gt;
